    "description": "The Checkout module publishes order operations through the Shop API while its pricing and inventory rules operate on PurchaseOrder, Money, and OrderLine domain types. The API boundary exposes separate request and response DTOs with ISO currency codes, minor-unit amounts, and flattened line identifiers. Both directions are active: HTTP requests become domain commands, and domain results become HTTP responses, including validation failures. Today, several controllers copy fields independently, so rounding rules and optional shipping data diverge between checkout and order-history endpoints. PurchaseOrder and its DTOs must remain independently deployable, and neither side may import the other. Establish one mapping component owned by Checkout that converts in both directions, keeps all amount and identifier rules there, and is exercised by contract tests whenever either representation changes.",
    "decision_statement": "Should Checkout use one bidirectional mapping owner between PurchaseOrder domain objects and Shop API DTOs, rather than repeating field-copying rules in each controller?",
    "notes": "converter fits the single bidirectional owner mapping PurchaseOrder domain objects to Shop API DTOs; message-translator is the wire-format reading of the same seam."
  },
